Z||000000||V8Fiero||05-03-2001||12:23 AM||||Got a line on a great deal on some tires and was wondering if anyone would know how/if they would fit.<P>My rims are 16 x 7.5<BR>Tires are 215/60-16<BR>Not too picky if it throws off the speedo. It is going on the V8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Scott||||reg||5
Z||000001||V8Fiero||05-03-2001||06:35 PM||||Anyone?<BR>Just want to make sure this tire would fit.<P>Thanks.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||05-04-2001||01:31 AM||||Im <I>pretty sure</I> that'll fit....Im kinda "iffy" on the 60 part, but I think it will fit.<BR>I try to avoid 16 inch wheels...dont care for em much. Too difficult to find decent tires for a good price...16 is kind of a funky size...usually go w/ 17s or 18s. <BR>I think tirerack or discount tire direct has a thing on their website that tells if a wheel will fit on a certain kind of car. If not, you CAN call them..its an 800 #. I did this with my 86 Gt when I went w/ 17 and 18s. They were helpful. Good luck! M7F||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||05-04-2001||02:03 AM||||They should work.  They'll be a little big in the wheel well, and your speedo will probably read a little slower than what you are really going.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gumball||05-04-2001||04:07 AM||||It fits. i once had the same configeration on my 86 SE.  The guys at Discount Tires installed little spacers to make sure the tires didn't hit the well or the rear sturt springs.||||reg||14
